Witness of linux-xa-store-range-ulong-max (lib/xarray.c, xa_store_range()).

  make LINUX=<kernel tree> harness   builds tools/testing/radix-tree once
  make LINUX=<kernel tree> run       exit 1 while the bug is there

Needs liburcu (URCU_PFX, default ~/.local/urcu_extract/usr).

Expected at v7.1 (8cd9520d35a6), checked 2026-11-07:
  xa_store_range(18446744073709551613, 18446744073709551614): ok
  xa_store_range(18446744073709551614, 18446744073709551615): BUG: did not return within 5 s
  xa_store_range(0, 18446744073709551615): BUG: did not return within 5 s
  exit 1

With candidate-fix.patch (the write-up's one-line fix: stop the tiling
loop when `first` wraps to 0), applied to v7.1 and the harness rebuilt:
  xa_store_range(18446744073709551613, 18446744073709551614): ok
  xa_store_range(18446744073709551614, 18446744073709551615): ok
  xa_store_range(0, 18446744073709551615): BUG: returned, but a load at an end of the range misses
  exit 1

So the candidate fix is incomplete.  Two paths reach the hang:
  - [ULONG_MAX - 1, ULONG_MAX]: the last chunk's size wraps `first` to 0;
  - [0, ULONG_MAX]: xas_set_range() sizes the single chunk 16 << 60 (shift
    60, 16 slots), so xas_size() is 0 and `first` never moves.
The fix stops both loops, but in the second case it stops after a store
that leaves ULONG_MAX empty.  Found 2026-11-07 by hegel-c's property test
(pin tests/irl/linux/pins/xa_store_range.conf, which shrinks to
[0, ULONG_MAX] on v7.1).  A real fix has to size or split that chunk.
